     "type": "concept",
     "title": "86 Billion Neurons",
     "content": "The brain is built from about 86 billion neurons, the special cells that carry electrical signals. Each neuron can connect to thousands of others, forming trillions of links. Neurons are the messengers, and their web of connections is where thinking, feeling, and remembering happen. That is more nerve cells than there are stars you could count in a lifetime.",
