     "content": "The wrinkled outer surface of the brain is called the cortex, the part that handles most of your conscious thinking. Those deep folds are not random, they let a large sheet of tissue fit inside a small skull. If you flattened the cortex it would spread out to about the size of a large pizza. More folds mean more surface, and more surface means more thinking power.",
