     "title": "Two Halves, One Bridge",
     "content": "The brain is split into two halves called hemispheres, a left and a right. They are joined in the middle by a thick band of fibers called the corpus callosum, which lets the two sides share information constantly. Think of it as a busy bridge carrying messages back and forth. The two halves are teammates, not rivals.",
